# Line endings: blobs are stored as LF and the working tree is checked out as
# LF on every platform. Without this, a Windows-side editor/tool that rewrites
# files with CRLF yields a whole-file diff with no semantic change (2026-11-04:
# 138 files, ~50k diff lines of pure CRLF noise). `text=auto` keeps git's
# binary detection, so images/archives are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The nightly ledger is append-only: concurrent nightly branches add distinct
# events at EOF. Plain git merges adjacent EOF insertions as a conflict, so use
# the built-in union driver to keep both lines (issue #566).
docs/dev/plans/nightly-ledger.jsonl merge=union
